---
import { article } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="on-pink" aria-labelledby="hc-h" style="background: #FF0088; color: #000">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top: clamp(64px, 8vw, 104px); padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 8vw, 104px); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 32px 64px; align-items: center">
    <div style="flex: 1 1 460px; min-width: 0; display: grid; gap: 18px">
      <p style="margin: 0; font-weight: 800; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase">Healthcare</p>
      <h2 id="hc-h" class="display" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px); line-height: 0.9">Yes, I film in clinics.</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 500; max-width: 48ch">I work in medical marketing every day. I know how to film in a clinic without slowing it down, keep patient information out of frame, and turn complicated care into short videos people actually finish.</p>
    </div>
    <a href={article.path} style="flex: 1 1 340px; max-width: 460px; background: #000; color: #FDFCF9; border-radius: 20px; padding: 28px; text-decoration: none; display: grid; gap: 14px">
      <span class="kicker">From the blog</span>
      <span class="display" style="font-size: 32px; line-height: 1">How to batch-film Instagram Reels for a medical clinic</span>
      <span style="font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 6px; color: #FF0088">Read the article</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
